title: Start
---
Welcome, to Mazes and Riddles!
You are a member of the local scouting club "The Cub Club".
Today you're on an excursion to a maze.
Your goal is to get to the end of the maze.
The maze has multiple colored doors, for which you must find the corresponding colored key!
To get a key, you must answer a riddle given to you by a colored instructor!
The instructors have hidden inside the maze.
Go find the instructor!
<<declare $currentRiddle = "BatteryRiddle">>
<<declare $currentInstructor = "NoInstructor">>
<<declare $answerredBlueCorrectly = "false">>
<<declare $answerredGreenCorrectly = "false">>
<<declare $answerredYellowCorrectly = "false">>
<<declare $answerredRedCorrectly = "false">>
<<declare $witnessedConflict = "false">>
<<declare $resolvedConflict = "false">>
===

//------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                  Instructor Selection
//------------------------------------------------------------------------

title: BlueInstructor
---
<<set $currentInstructor to "BlueInstructor">>
<<if $answerredBlueCorrectly == "true">>
    Meryl: Hello again!
    Meryl: You already got my key!
    Meryl: I have no more riddles for you.
    Meryl: Good luck finding the other instructors!
<<else>>
    Meryl: Hello!
    Meryl: I am the Blue Instructor.
    Meryl: If you get this upcoming riddle correct, I'll give you the blue key.
    <<jump SelectRiddle>>
<<endif>>
===

title: GreenInstructor
---
<<set $currentInstructor to "GreenInstructor">>
Jan: Hey-Hi! You found me!
<<if $answerredGreenCorrectly == "true">>
    Jan: Oh, it's you again!
    Jan: I have no more riddles for you, you know.
    Jan: Go find the other instructors!
<<else>>
    Jan: Yes, I am the Green Instructor.
    Jan: I have a little riddle for you.
    <<jump SelectRiddle>>
<<endif>>
===

title: YellowInstructor
---
<<set $currentInstructor to "YellowInstructor">>
Dave: Oh, it's you! Hello there.
<<if $answerredYellowCorrectly == "true">>
    Dave: You already got my key!
    Dave: I have no more riddles for you.
    Dave: Good luck finding the other instructors!
<<else>>
    <<if $witnessedConflict == "true">>
        ->Ask about Gerald.
            <<jump YellowInstructorConflict>>
        ->Ask for the riddle.
            Dave: Are you ready for this riddle?
            <<jump SelectRiddle>>
    <<else>>
        Dave: I am the yellow instructor today.
        Dave: Are you ready for this riddle?
        <<jump SelectRiddle>>
    <<endif>>
<<endif>>
===

title: YellowInstructorConflict
---
Dave: Oh, did you overhear?
Dave: I am so sorry about that.
Dave: Gerald just isn't himself today.
Dave: I have an idea.
Dave: Here's a snickers.
<<give_item "Player" "Snickers">>
You received a snickers bar.
Dave: Give it to Gerald, will you?
Dave: Oh, and let's not forget about the riddle. Here it is.
<<jump SelectRiddle>>
===

title: RedInstructor
---
<<if $resolvedConflict == "true">>
    <<if $answerredRedCorrectly == "true">>
        Gerald: Hey kid! You already got my key.
        Gerald: Go get out of the maze, haha.
    <<else>>
        Gerald: Hey kid! Thanks again for the snickers.
        Gerald: Are you ready for the riddle? This one is really difficult.
        <<jump SelectRiddle>>
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    <<set $currentInstructor to "RedInstructor">>
    <<if $answerredRedCorrectly == "true">>
        Gerald: You already got my key, did you forget?
        Gerald: Go find the other instructors or something.
    <<else>>
        Gerald: Hmph. Took you long enough.
        Gerald: Did you get lost or something?
        <<if has_item("Player", "Snickers")>>
            ->Ask if Gerald is okay.
                <<jump RedInstructorConflict>>
            ->Apologize for getting lost and ask for the riddle.
                Gerald: You better be ready for this riddle.
                <<jump SelectRiddle>>
        <<else>>
            Gerald: You better be ready for this riddle.
            <<jump SelectRiddle>>
        <<endif>>
    <<endif>>
<<endif>>
===

title: RedInstructorConflict
---
Gerald: Yeah, why wouldn't I be fine?
->Tell him Dave wanted him to have this Snickers
    <<set $resolvedConflict to "true">>
    Gerald: He thought of me?
    Gerald: That's... So nice.
    Gerald: Thank you.
    Gerald: You know what, in return, you don't have to answer my riddle.
    Gerald: Here's my key!
    You received the Red Key!
    <<give_item "Player" "RedKey">>
    <<set $answerredRedCorrectly to "true">>
    Gerald: Now go get out of the maze, haha.
->Say nothing.
    Gerald: You better be ready for this riddle.
    <<jump SelectRiddle>>
===

//------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                  Riddle Selection
//------------------------------------------------------------------------

title: SelectRiddle
---
<<if $currentInstructor == "BlueInstructor">>
    <<jump EasyRiddle>>
<<elseif $currentInstructor == "GreenInstructor">>
    <<jump MediumRiddle>>
<<elseif $currentInstructor == "YellowInstructor">>
    <<jump HardRiddle>>
<<elseif $currentInstructor == "RedInstructor">>
    <<jump VeryHardRiddle>>
<<endif>>
===

title: EasyRiddle
---
<<if $currentRiddle == "BatteryRiddle">>
    <<jump BatteryRiddle>>
<<elseif $currentRiddle == "DoorbellRiddle">>
    <<jump DoorbellRiddle>>
<<else>>
    <<set $currentRiddle to "BatteryRiddle">>
    <<jump EasyRiddle>>
<<endif>>
===

title: MediumRiddle
---
<<if $currentRiddle == "ClockRiddle">>
    <<jump ClockRiddle>>
<<elseif $currentRiddle == "SecretRiddle">>
    <<jump SecretRiddle>>
<<elseif $currentRiddle == "CloudRiddle">>
    <<jump CloudRiddle>>
<<elseif $currentRiddle == "MapRiddle">>
    <<jump MapRiddle>>
<<else>>
    <<set $currentRiddle to "ClockRiddle">>
    <<jump MediumRiddle>>
<<endif>>
===

title: HardRiddle
---
<<if $currentRiddle == "FireRiddle">>
    <<jump FireRiddle>>
<<elseif $currentRiddle == "MirrorRiddle">>
    <<jump MirrorRiddle>>
<<elseif $currentRiddle == "BreathRiddle">>
    <<jump BreathRiddle>>
<<elseif $currentRiddle == "HoleRiddle">>
    <<jump HoleRiddle>>
<<else>>
    <<set $currentRiddle to "FireRiddle">>
    <<jump HardRiddle>>
<<endif>>
===

title: VeryHardRiddle
---
<<if $currentRiddle == "ERiddle">>
    <<jump ERiddle>>
<<else>>
    <<set $currentRiddle to "ERiddle">>
    <<jump VeryHardRiddle>>
<<endif>>
===



//------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                  Easy Riddles
//------------------------------------------------------------------------

title: BatteryRiddle
---
I have no life, but I can die, what am I?
<<set $currentRiddle to "DoorbellRiddle">>
->A battery
    <<jump CorrectAnswer>>
->A mug
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
->A phone
    <<jump CorrectAnswer>>
===

title: DoorbellRiddle
---
I never ask questions, but I am always answered, what am I?
<<set $currentRiddle to "FireRiddle">>
->A call
    <<jump CorrectAnswer>>
->A doorbell
    <<jump CorrectAnswer>>
->A joke
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
===

//------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                  Medium Riddles
//------------------------------------------------------------------------

title: ClockRiddle
---
I have two hands, but I can not scratch myself. Even when dead, I am right twice a day. What am I?
<<set $currentRiddle to "SecretRiddle">>
->A clock
    <<jump CorrectAnswer>>
->A doll
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
->A scarecrow
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
===

title: SecretRiddle
---
The more of me you share, the less of me you have. What am I?
<<set $currentRiddle to "CloudRiddle">>
->Happiness
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
->A memory
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
->A secret
    <<jump CorrectAnswer>>
===

title: CloudRiddle
---
I can fly without wings, cry without eyes, and whenever I go, darkness flies. What am I?
<<set $currentRiddle to "MapRiddle">>
->A bird
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
->A cloud
    <<jump CorrectAnswer>>
->A comet
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
===

title: MapRiddle
---
I have cities, but no houses; mountains, but no snow; water, but no fish. What am I?
<<set $currentRiddle to "ClockRiddle">>
->A desert
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
->An illusion
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
->A map
    <<jump CorrectAnswer>>
===

//------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                  Hard Riddles
//------------------------------------------------------------------------

title: FireRiddle
---
    I am not alive, but I grow; I don't have lungs, but I need air; I don't have a mouth, but water kills me. What am I?
<<set $currentRiddle to "MirrorRiddle">>
->A cloud
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
->A fire
    <<jump CorrectAnswer>>
->Rust
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
===

title: MirrorRiddle
---
I make two people out of one. What am I?
<<set $currentRiddle to "BreathRiddle">>
->A mask
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
->A mirror
    <<jump CorrectAnswer>>
->A shadow
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
===

title: BreathRiddle
---
I am as light as a feather, yet no man can hold me for long. What am I?
<<set $currentRiddle to "HoleRiddle">>
->A breath
    <<jump CorrectAnswer>>
->A secret
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
->Time
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
===

title: HoleRiddle
---
The more you take from me, the bigger I get. What am I?
<<set $currentRiddle to "FireRiddle">>
->A hole
    <<jump CorrectAnswer>>
->A pocket
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
->Silence
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
===

//------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                  Very Hard Riddles
//------------------------------------------------------------------------

title: ERiddle
---
I am the beginning of the end, and the end of time and space. I am essential to creation, and I surround every place. What am I?
<<set $currentRiddle to "ERiddle">>
->Darkness
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
->Infinity
    <<jump WrongAnswer>>
->The letter E
    <<jump CorrectAnswer>>
===

//------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                  Answers
//------------------------------------------------------------------------

title: CorrectAnswer
---

<<if $currentInstructor == "BlueInstructor">>
    Meryl: That was correct.
    Meryl: Here is the key I promised.
    You received the Blue Key!
    <<give_item "Player" "BlueKey">>
    <<set $answerredBlueCorrectly to "true">>
<<elseif $currentInstructor == "GreenInstructor">>
    Jan: That is absolutely correct!
    Jan: Well done!
    Jan: Here's a little somethin.
    You received the Green Key!
    <<give_item "Player" "GreenKey">>
    <<set $answerredGreenCorrectly to "true">>
<<elseif $currentInstructor == "YellowInstructor">>
    Dave: Good job!
    Dave: That was correct.
    Dave: Here is the key.
    You received the Yellow Key!
    <<give_item "Player" "YellowKey">>
    <<set $answerredYellowCorrectly to "true">>
<<elseif $currentInstructor == "RedInstructor">>
    Gerald: I guess you know something after all.
    Gerald: Here. Now don't waste my time further.
    You received the Red Key!
    <<give_item "Player" "RedKey">>
    <<set $answerredRedCorrectly to "true">>
<<endif>>
===

title: WrongAnswer
---
<<if $currentInstructor == "BlueInstructor">>
    Meryl: That was wrong!
    Meryl: I have another riddle for you to try again on.
<<elseif $currentInstructor == "GreenInstructor">>
    Jan: Uh-oh, that was unfortunately not correct.
    Jan: I have another riddle for you to try again, though!
<<elseif $currentInstructor == "YellowInstructor">>
    Dave: Sorry, but that was wrong.
    Dave: Here, please try again with this new riddle.
<<elseif $currentInstructor == "RedInstructor">>
    Gerald: No, no, no. That was wrong.
    Gerald: Try. Again.
<<endif>>
<<jump SelectRiddle>>
===

//------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                  Doors
//------------------------------------------------------------------------

title: BlueDoor
---
You approach the Blue Door.
<<if has_item("Player", "BlueKey")>>
    You have the key!
    <<play_animation "BlueDoor" "OpenDoor">>
    <<take_item "Player" "BlueKey">>
    The door opens.
<<else>>
    The door is locked.
    You seem to need a Blue Key to open this door.
    Maybe you can get it from the Blue Instructor?
<<endif>>
===

title: GreenDoor
---
You approach the Green Door.
<<if has_item("Player", "GreenKey")>>
    You have the key!
    <<play_animation "GreenDoor" "OpenDoor">>
    <<take_item "Player" "GreenKey">>
    The door opens.
<<else>>
    The door is locked.
    You seem to need a Green Key to open this door.
    Maybe you can get it from the Green Instructor?
<<endif>>
===

title: YellowDoor
---
You approach the Yellow Door.
<<if has_item("Player", "YellowKey")>>
    You have the key!
    <<play_animation "YellowDoor" "OpenDoor">>
    <<take_item "Player" "YellowKey">>
    The door opens.
<<else>>
    The door is locked.
    You seem to need a Yellow Key to open this door.
    Maybe you can get it from the Yellow Instructor?
<<endif>>
===

title: RedDoor
---
You approach the Red Door.
<<if has_item("Player", "RedKey")>>
    You have the key!
    <<play_animation "RedDoor" "OpenDoor">>
    <<take_item "Player" "RedKey">>
    The door opens.
<<else>>
    The door is locked.
    You seem to need a Red Key to open this door.
    Maybe you can get it from the Red Instructor?
<<endif>>
===

//------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                  Conflict
//------------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Conflict
---
When you approach the doors, you hear faint shouting in the distance.
Gerald: I'm done.
Dave: Don't be too hasty, Gerald.
Gerald: No. These kids just can't get anything right and it's so frustrating, Dave!
Dave: But you signed up for this event, and you have to see it through until all the kids-
Gerald interrupts Dave.
Gerald: What are you gonna do? Stop me from walking out of this maze?
Dave: If I have to, I will. Now get back to your spot, Gerald.
It's quiet for a moment.
Gerald: ...
Gerald: Fine. But I am going to quit after this.
<<set $witnessedConflict to "true">>
===

//------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                  End Level
//------------------------------------------------------------------------

title: EndLevel
---
Congratulations!
You made it to the end.
You have solved all riddles and collected all keys!
You have earned your Navigation Badge!
<<if $resolvedConflict == "true">>
    Gerald was feeling much better after you gave him the snickers.
    He gave you a special badge for helping another person.
<<else>>
    Sadly, since you didn't help Gerald, he ended up quitting the Cub Club.
    After losing an instructor, the morale of the club dropped significantly.
    This would be the last excursion you went on for a while.
<<endif>>
===